{
  "name": "Google Sheets content calendar to Preflight, checked before scheduling",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Google Sheets content calendar → Preflight\n\nWrite posts in a sheet, set **Status** to `Ready`, and every 15 minutes they are checked against each network's rules and scheduled in Preflight. The row gets the Preflight post ID and `Scheduled`, or `Needs fix` with the exact reason (e.g. \"24 characters over on Bluesky\").\n\n**Sheet columns**\n`Text | Channels | Publish At | Media URL | Link | Status | Preflight Post ID | Issues`\n\n- **Channels**: network names, comma-separated, e.g. `bluesky, mastodon, linkedin` (or `platform:channelId` when you have two of one network).\n- **Publish At**: `2026-11-02 09:30` in the workflow's time zone. Empty = next free queue slot.\n- **Media URL**: optional public link to an image or video.\n\nPick the sheet in all three Google Sheets nodes and your Preflight credential in the Preflight nodes.",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 500
      },
      "id": "0852f8e6-61e8-5745-a1f2-d7fc4dfdbdcb",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        -300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "minutes",
              "minutesInterval": 15
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "557f7527-9d2f-5db9-96ec-991ed8d759fa",
      "name": "Every 15 minutes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
